    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "The meaning of the terms encoding, storage and retrieval are as follows: (i) Encoding - It refers to the first stage of memory in which information is recorded and registered for the first time. (ii) Storage - It is the second stage of memory in which the encoded information is stored and retained over a period of time. (iii) Retrieval - It is the third stage and refers to bringing the stored information into awareness.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, encoding, storage, and retrieval are the three essential stages of memory.",
